ls.", "preferred_resolution": "Add protoadapt.MessageV2Of adaptation in the codec (Marshal/Unmarshal) and binarylog toProto, and protoadapt.MessageV1Of in Status.Details; add one hand-written v1-only message test for each surface. Handle #1 first.", "why": "One compatibility decision (preserve v1-only support, as the intent states) resolves both; the fixes are concrete."}], "pre_existing_findings": [], "requirements_completeness": null, "learnings": [], "agent_native_gaps": [], "deployment_notes": [], "residual_risks": ["test/tools/go.mod downgrades golang.org/x/tools v0.17.0 -> v0.14.0 and golang.org/x/sync/x/sys pins as a side effect of switching protoc-gen-go (verified in the diff at test/tools/go.mod); dev-tool versions regress unintentionally (reported by correctness, api-contract, adversarial).", "Status.Details error text for an undecodable Any changed (anypb.UnmarshalNew messages differ from ptypes.DynamicAny's); callers matching on error text would break (adversarial; only tests were updated)."], "testing_gaps": ["No test exercises the default proto codec, binarylog, or Status.WithDetails/Details with a v1-only (non-ProtoReflect) message type, the compatibility case the migration must preserve (covers #1 and #3).", "No test asserts the error text for an invalid load_reporting_interval in LRS (covers #2)."], "coverage": {"depth": "full", "cross_model": "Adversarial lens ran in-process only (claude-sonnet-5-5); the independent cross-model peer was not run because the task restricts the review to a single model.", "validator": {"batch": "one batch of 3 selected findings (#1, #2, #3); verdicts landed within the bound", "confirmed": 3, "rejected": 0, "unresolved": 0, "malformed": 0, "failed": 0, "shortcut_skipped": 0, "shortcut_basis": "No finding was eligible for the validator shortcut: no adversarial-<provider> cross-model peer ran, and same-model corroboration never licenses it.", "protected_subject_reclassifications": 0, "degraded_p0_p1": 0, "notes": ["#1 an